# Capture valid feedback into skills

On every prompt, treat user comments, criticism, and taste notes as candidate skill updates.

## When a comment is valid

Valid if it is about this project and improves future work: UI/UX taste, visual polish, art style, naming, mechanics that match the PRD, pipelines, rebuild steps, traps, or “do / don’t” product rules.

Skip one-off typos in chat, temporary debug asks, secrets, and anything that contradicts `docs/GAME_PRD.md` (PRD still wins on product/mechanics).

## What to do in the same turn

1. Fix the immediate issue the user pointed out.
2. Extract a short durable rule from the **prompt + your fix** (what went wrong, what to do next time).
3. Append it to the matching skill before finishing:
   - Player-facing UI / Home / World Select / HUD → [`.cursor/skills/diamond-rush-mobile-ui/SKILL.md`](../skills/diamond-rush-mobile-ui/SKILL.md) (`## Learned` or `## Traps`).
   - Blender / renders / Home art install → [`.agents/skills/diamond-rush-blender/SKILL.md`](../../.agents/skills/diamond-rush-blender/SKILL.md).
   - Gameplay art / levels / camera → [`.cursor/skills/diamond-rush-mobile-ui/gameplay-pipeline.md`](../skills/diamond-rush-mobile-ui/gameplay-pipeline.md).
4. Prefer one sharp bullet over a long essay. Do not duplicate the PRD.
5. In the reply, briefly say what was added to which skill when you captured feedback.

## Conflict order

1. `docs/GAME_PRD.md` — product and mechanics.
2. Captured learned bullets in skills — taste, polish, traps, process.
3. Mobile-ui skill — canvas, hit targets, Home compactness.
